<h1>Gap and Flush</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">T</span><span lang="EN-US">he</span> <span lang="EN-US" class="Command">Gap and Flush</span> <span class="Command">mode</span> <span lang="EN-US">command is accessible from</span> <b><i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Measure &gt; Gap and Flush</b></span></i></b><span lang="EN-US">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">This command switches the mode for creating Gap and Flush dimensions. For the moment Gap and Flush dimensions in KUBE represent distances between point and line defined by two points. Points can be picked from vertices of compound entities or from feature points of datums &#160;In this mode a <u><a href="../User_Interface/Measure_Context_Menus.htm#Viewport_GapFlush">context menu</a></u> appears when clicking on a Gap and Flush dimension with the RMB, offering modifying, deletion of current or all Gap and Flush dimensions.</span></p>
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US">I</span>n any given process there will be an ideal separation (gap) and ideal relative depth (flush) that was specified at design time. The manufactured product however will deviate from this ideal by a varying amount. The figure below gives a cross section through two flat surfaces, showing the definition of Gap and Flush:</p>
<p class="bullet"><img src="../Measure/images/Gap_Flush_scheme.gif" width="700px" height="297px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="bullet">The Gap and Flush mode provides a manual way of measuring the relative position of two panels in an assembled product. This tool works best on sections across the panels.</p>
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US">When this mode is enabled the cursor changes to Gap and Flush tool <img src="../Measure/images/gap_flush_cursor1.gif" width="23px" height="26px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""> &#160;for picking the first point, <img src="../Measure/images/gap_flush_cursor2.gif" width="23px" height="26px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""> &#160;for picking the second point, or <img src="../Measure/images/gap_flush_cursor3.gif" width="23px" height="26px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""> &#160;for picking the third point. Click on a point from compound entity (scan data, mesh, point cloud, probe points, polyline) or feature point of a datum (line start point, sphere centre, etc.) to define the first point from the infinite line. Then click on a point to define the second point from the infinite line. Finally click on a point to define the distance from this point to the infinite line. While holding the left mouse button move the mouse cursor to the position where you want to place the Gap and Flush dimension.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial; text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a4" style="text-decoration:underline;">Gap and Flush example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP165890522" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<table cellspacing="0" width="100%" class="whs6">
<col class="whs7">
<tr valign="top" class="whs8">
<td width="100%" class="whs9">
<p><img src="../Measure/images/gap_flush_example1.gif" width="746px" height="300px" border="0" class="img_whs10" alt=""></p>
<p>Two panels surface with extracted parallel polylines</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs8">
<td width="100%" class="whs11">
<p><img src="../Measure/images/gap_flush_example2.gif" width="746px" height="300px" border="0" class="img_whs10" alt=""></p>
<p>Flush measured from one of the polylines</p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p>&#160;</p>
</div>
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US">Gap and Flush dimensions consist of line with arrows in both ends, value in the centre of the line, and two limiting lines. If fitted the value is in the centre of the dimension line, otherwise it is automatically carried on left, top, or bottom of the line depending on the particular situation.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial; text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a3" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP165335600" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../Measure/images/gap_flush_example3.gif" width="671px" height="469px" border="0" class="img_whs12" alt=""><br>
<br>
Gap and Flush dimension value outside the line (top) and within the line (bottom)</p>
</div>
<p class="bullet" style="font-weight:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">When you pass over the value of an existing Gap and Flush dimension line the cursor changes its shape to <img src="../Measure/images/hand_cursor.gif" width="22px" height="26px" border="0" class="img_whs13" alt=""> To modify dimension line position, just click on it and drag the line to the position you want.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial; text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2" style="text-decoration:underline;">Move Gap and Flush dimension example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP165149558" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../Measure/images/move_gap_flush.gif" width="337px" height="193px" border="0" class="img_whs14" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p class="bullet" style="font-weight:normal;"><b style="font-weight:normal;"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:normal;">To modify all Gap and Flush dimensions right click on a Gap and Flush dimension and select Modify from the Context menu or go to</span> <span style="font-style:italic;"><i><a href="Preferences_-_Display_-_Dimensions.htm">Preferences &gt; Display &gt; Dimensions</a></i></span> <span class="Command" style="font-weight:normal;">dialog.</span></b></p>
<p class="bullet" style="font-weight:normal;"><b><span class="Command" style="font-weight:normal;">Gap and Flush dimensions can be deleted individually or all at once. To delete individual Gap and Flush dimension right-click on it and from the context menu select <a href="Delete_Gap_and_Flush.htm">Delete Gap and Flush</a> command.</span></b></p>
<p class="bullet" style="font-weight:normal;"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:normal;">To delete all Gap and Flush dimensions in the s</span><span class="Command" style="font-weight:normal;">cene</span></b> <b><span class="Command" style="font-weight:normal;">right-click on a Gap and Flush dimension value and from the context menu select</span> <span class="Command"><a href="delete_all_gap_and_flush.htm" style="font-weight:normal;">Delete All Gap and Flush</a></span> <span style="font-weight:normal;">command or</span></b> go to Measure menu and select the same command from there.</p>
<p class="Note" id="P2"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: When an entity (or both entities) used for dimensioning is hidden then all Gap and Flush dimensions related to that entity (entities) are also hidden.</p>
<p class="Warning">Gap and Flush dimensions and their positions are stored in the sab2 file so next time you open it all created dimensions appear. Formatting is not stored so when you open the file, the Gap and Flush dimensions will be formatted with their default settings.</p>
